.TH PMX "1" "November 2026" "PMXViewer v0.2.1+GLFW3.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pmx \- MikuMikuDance PMX/PMD model / VMD motion viewer (MikuMikuPenguin)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pmx
[\fB\-s\fR \fImusic\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fIcamera.vmd\fR] [\fB\-l\fR \fIlight.vmd\fR] [\fB\-\-loop\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-gui\fR] [\fB\-\-effect\fR \fIlist\fR] [\fB\-\-dof\-focus\fR \fIdistance\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR \fIB,C,S,G\fR] {\fImodel.pmx\fR|\fImodel.pmd\fR} [\fImotion.vmd\fR] [\fB\-\-pos\fR \fIX,Y,Z\fR] [\fImodel2\fR [\fImotion2.vmd\fR] ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pmx
(PMXViewer) is a demonstration program for the MikuMikuPenguin library
(libmmp).  It loads a PMX 2.0 or PMD model and plays a VMD motion on it, with
Bullet physics for hair, skirts and other rigid bodies.
Camera and light motion are played, and the model visibility and IK on/off
keys of the motion file are honoured.  Like MMD, the model casts a ground
shadow and a self shadow (shadow map) following the light.
.PP
An OpenGL 3.2 core profile capable driver is required.
.PP
Several models can be played together: each VMD file belongs to the model
given before it (a model without a VMD stays in its rest pose).  All models
share the time line, the camera and the light; each has its own physics
(models do not collide with each other).  Motions made for several dancers
usually contain each dancer's position already.
.PP
Files can also be opened while the viewer runs: from \fBFile\fR on the
playback bar (add a model, a motion for a model, camera or light motion,
music), from the settings panel (motion / remove for each model), or by
dropping them onto the window (PMX/PMD = add a model, VMD = motion for the
first model without one, or camera/light motion when the VMD has no bone or
morph keys, other files = music).  Without file arguments the viewer starts
empty.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-pos\fR \fIX,Y,Z\fR
Position of the preceding model, in MMD coordinates (also adjustable in the
settings panel).
.TP
\fB\-s\fR \fIfile\fR
Play a music file along with the VMD motion.
Only formats supported by SDL2_mixer are accepted.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR \fIfile\fR
Camera motion (a VMD file with camera frames).  Without this option the
camera frames contained in the motion file, if any, are used.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR \fIfile\fR
Light motion (a VMD file with light frames).  Without this option the light
frames of the \fB\-c\fR file are used, then those of the motion file.
.TP
\fB\-\-loop\fR
Restart from the beginning when the end of the motion (its last key) is
reached.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-gui\fR
Start with the on-screen controls hidden (\fBTab\fR shows them).
.TP
\fB\-\-effect\fR \fIlist\fR
Turn on screen effects (see \fBSCREEN EFFECTS\fR); \fIlist\fR is a comma
separated list of \fBbloom\fR, \fBglow\fR (also \fBal\fR, \fBautoluminous\fR),
\fBdof\fR, \fBssao\fR, \fBcolor\fR, \fBfxaa\fR, \fBall\fR and \fBnone\fR.
\fIname\fB=\fIvalue\fR also sets the main strength of an effect: the
intensity of bloom and glow, the strength of the depth of field and of SSAO.
Example: \fB\-\-effect bloom=1.2,dof\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-dof\-focus\fR \fIdistance\fR
Turn the depth of field on with a fixed focus distance (MMD units from the
camera) instead of the camera's point of interest.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fIB,C,S,G\fR
Turn colour correction on with brightness (added, default 0), contrast
(default 1), saturation (default 1) and gamma (default 1; above 1 brightens
the mid tones).  Trailing values may be left out.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
display help and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
output version information and exit
.SH CONTROLS
A playback bar (play/pause, seek, frame step, timeline, loop) is shown at the
bottom of the window, and its \fBSettings\fR button opens a panel with the
display options and a list of these shortcuts.  The labels are Japanese when
the locale is Japanese and a Japanese font is installed.
.TP
.B Tab
show / hide the on-screen controls
.TP
.B Left mouse drag
rotate the camera
.TP
.B Mouse wheel
zoom in / out
.TP
.B Up / Down
move the model up / down
.TP
.B Q (hold)
pause the physics simulation
.TP
.B A (hold)
hide the model
.TP
.B S, D, F, G (hold)
Bullet debug drawing (wireframe, AABB, constraints, constraint limits)
.TP
.B C
toggle the VMD camera motion (moving the camera with the mouse switches to the free camera)
.TP
.B Space
pause / resume (the music too)
.TP
.B Left / Right
seek 1 second back / forward (with Shift: 10 seconds); the physics restarts
from the new pose
.TP
.B , / .
one frame back / forward (pauses playback)
.TP
.B Home / End
go to the beginning / end of the motion
.TP
.B O
toggle looping
.TP
.B Z
toggle the ground shadow
.TP
.B X
toggle the self shadow (also switched by the self shadow keys of the VMD)
.TP
.B L
toggle the VMD light motion (off: MMD default light)
.TP
.B R
reset the camera (front view framing the whole model)
.TP
.B Esc
quit
.SH SCREEN EFFECTS
The viewer can add looks that MMD users get from MME (MikuMikuEffect)
effects; no .fx files are read.  With any effect on, the scene is drawn into
a floating point offscreen framebuffer (multisampled like the window, with
depth and stencil), processed by full-screen passes and then shown; the
on-screen controls are drawn afterwards.  All effects are off at start, and
while they are off the scene is drawn directly into the window as before.
They are turned on and adjusted in the \fBEffects\fR section of the settings
panel, or with \fB\-\-effect\fR.
.TP
.B Bloom
Parts brighter than the threshold (luminance 0\-1) bleed into their
surroundings.  Settings: intensity, threshold, spread.
.TP
.B Glow (AutoLuminous-like)
Materials with a specular power (reflection strength) of 110 or more emit
light in their own colour, more for higher values, as with AutoLuminous.
Optionally the brightest parts of the models (luminance above a threshold)
glow too.  The light spreads like the bloom.  Settings: intensity, bright
parts on/off and threshold.
.TP
.B Depth of field
Blurs what is nearer or farther than the focus distance.  The focus follows
the camera's point of interest by default (the interest point of the camera
motion; the orbit centre of the free camera), or is set by hand.  Settings:
focus distance, strength (how fast things blur away from the focus), maximum
blur (1 = 1/40 of the picture height).
.TP
.B SSAO
Screen-space ambient occlusion: darkens creases and places hidden from the
open space.  Settings: strength, radius (MMD units).
.TP
.B Colour correction
Brightness, contrast, saturation and gamma of the final picture.
.TP
.B FXAA
Fast approximate anti-aliasing of the final picture.
.PP
SSAO, the depth of field blur and the bloom are computed at half resolution
or below, and effects that are off are skipped.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/mikumikupenguin/shaders/
GLSL shaders, with the screen effects in \fIpostfx/\fR (a \fIshaders/\fR
directory in the current directory takes precedence).
.TP
.I /usr/share/mikumikupenguin/textures/
shared toon textures toon01.bmp \- toon10.bmp.
.TP
.I /usr/share/mikumikupenguin/doc/README_JP.html
Japanese documentation.
